38 #edb/ref 17592186399621 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186119844 1038 #edb/ref 17592186399628 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186119890 1038 #edb/ref 17592186399600 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186124613 1038 #edb/ref 17592186399523 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186124661 1038 #edb/ref 17592186399474 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186124661 1038 #edb/ref 17592186399481 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186129103 1038 #edb/ref 17592186399446 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186129103 1038 #edb/ref 17592186399453 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186129123 1038 #edb/ref 17592186399488 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186133962 1038 #edb/ref 17592186399495 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186152193 1038 #edb/ref 17592186399516 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186152195 1038 #edb/ref 17592186399537 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186172030 1038 #edb/ref 17592186399363 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186175954 1038 #edb/ref 17592186399390 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186175970 1038 #edb/ref 17592186399432 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186175982 1038 #edb/ref 17592186399439 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186176059 1038 #edb/ref 17592186399404 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186176185 1068 #edb/ref 17592186173338 13194139533478 17592186045585 false] [17592186176185 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399384 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186176185 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186176185 1071 "What surface is defined by the equation $r = 3$ in cylindrical polar coordinates?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 false] [17592186176185 1071 "What surface is defined by the equation $r=3$ in cylindrical polar coordinates?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186176185 1074 "The position of a point in cylindrical polar coordinates is written as $(r,\\theta ,z),$ where \n\n- $r\\ge 0$ and $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi )$ are the usual plane polar coordinates, and\n\n- $z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ is the usual Cartesian $z$-coordinate.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our equation:\n\n$$\nr=3\n$$\n\nThis equation requires that the distance from any point on the surface to the $z$-axis equals $3,$ while $\\theta $ and $z$ can vary arbitrarily in their respective domains. \n\nTherefore, our surface is the circular cylinder shown below.\n\n![](images/aa/aa435c0ad4b4482c85a05af32afbbb7819b330a4292762ec66bad30a6ed31a44.png)" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186184173 1038 #edb/ref 17592186399593 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399356 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399357 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399356 1069 "q-101736" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399356 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399356 1071 "Which of the following improper integrals are divergent?\n\nI. ${\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(u-1)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}u$\nII. ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1}3{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z$\nIII. ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399356 1072 #uuid "79e7ca1d-1ed8-5888-8523-0ec8ed90db1c" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399356 1074 "Let's work out each integral.\n\nFor the first integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(u-1)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}u & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{2}^{a}\\frac{1}{(u-1)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{2(u-1)^{2}}]}_{2}^{a} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(-\\frac{1}{2(a-1)^{2}}+\\frac{1}{2(2-1)^{2}}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2(a-1)^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the integral is convergent.\n\nFor the second integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1}3{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{1}3{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[{z}^{3}]}_{a}^{1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(1-{a}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\infty ,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the integral diverges.\n\nFor the third integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{-2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{x}]}_{a}^{-2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the integral is convergent.\n\nIn conclusion, only integral II is divergent." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399357 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399358 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399357 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399359 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399357 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399360 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399357 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399361 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399357 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399362 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399357 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399357 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399357 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399362 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399357 1080 #uuid "027a26b9-e238-53ff-b245-735c0d2abc04" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399358 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399358 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399358 1084 #uuid "c286d992-e374-59ca-b86a-46b1f01569c8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399359 1081 "I only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399359 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399359 1084 #uuid "aa7fc32d-93c3-5f24-9422-4d81ca03151b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399360 1081 "III only" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399360 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 131941