}⁡(3\\theta )$ for $\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{5\\pi }{6}$ (shown in blue in the diagram above)?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399411 1072 #uuid "fff3852c-f58f-5d0e-926d-65e98b09f1bd" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399411 1074 "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta ),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\theta ).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta ))^{2}+(-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\theta ))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{16{cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )+144{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{16({cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )+9{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta ))}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )+9{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399412 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399413 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399412 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399414 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399412 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399415 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399412 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399416 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399412 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399417 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399412 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399412 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399412 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399416 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399412 1080 #uuid "f5c70003-7fda-53ca-a766-8fe5b6a753c4" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399413 1081 "\\frac{3}{4}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )+{cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399413 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399413 1084 #uuid "c6874921-2d2f-5f05-b3f8-8b581a1d8844" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399414 1081 "4{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )-{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399414 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399414 1084 #uuid "ed64815a-d2d8-553b-a6f7-b8434bf21b56" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399415 1081 "\\frac{4}{3}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )+9{cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399415 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399415 1084 #uuid "98fb496d-54bd-55f2-a700-7d72677cb636" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399416 1081 "4{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )+9{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399416 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399416 1084 #uuid "bdb7b1c9-29a2-5223-81e5-94639a44cc1d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399417 1081 "3{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )-3{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399417 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399417 1084 #uuid "83e1d477-bc0c-53ce-bc7e-6ddda95d6630" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399418 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399419 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399418 1069 "q-103892" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399418 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399418 1071 "Find the radius and center of the circle whose equation is\n${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+7x=0.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399418 1072 #uuid "3f6a0f67-fd62-5333-8099-37761d6fc395" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399418 1074 "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+7x & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+7x)+{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}x+{(\\frac{7}{2})}^{2})+{y}^{2} & ={(\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect square and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(x+\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={(\\frac{7}{2})}^{2} \\\\ {(x-(-\\frac{7}{2}))}^{2}+(y-0)^{2} & ={(\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(-\\frac{7}{2},0)$ and its radius is $\\frac{7}{2}.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399419 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399420 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399419 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399421 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399419 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399422 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399419 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399423 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399419 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399424 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399419 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399419 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399419 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399421 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399419 1080 #uuid "4c479e6f-23bb-5fd5-ab28-ff2cfcd0fb64" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399420 1081 "center: $(-7,0)$, radius: $49$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399420 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399420 1084 #uuid "6b34439c-2388-5711-9ac8-63f5bf3cf549" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399421 1081 "center: $(-\\frac{7}{2},0)$, radius: $\\frac{7}{2}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399421 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399421 1084 #uuid "1eb48f02-d998-5b04-842c-b869161eadb6" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399422 1081 "center: $(-\\frac{7}{2},0)$, radius: $\\frac{7}{4}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399422 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399422 1084 #uuid "317341c2-5258-5001-88cf-9b017288ada7" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399423 1081 "center: $(\\frac{7}{2},0)$, radius: $\\frac{7}{2}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399423 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399423 1084 #uuid "f3bcc4ce-6ce1-5ebf-8946-9df961f73342" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399424 1081 "center: $(7,0)$, radius: $7$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399424 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399424 1084 #uuid "1ed03bf8-4e63-5262-8883-5b8d87a82e28" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399425 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399426 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399425 1069 "q-104195" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399425 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399425 1071 "A gardener wants to fence a rectangular flowerbed with $15$ meters of fencing. To two decimal places, what is the largest area that he can make with the fencing?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399425 1072 #uuid "1af9295c-5eff-510e-ba44-71a6e28cc19c" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399425 1074 "**Step 1**: Let us call $x$ and $y$ the dimensions of the rectangle.\n\n![](images/be/bebb7c4ca5e38d75136146f6e4547b0e72d529ce24453a3d0212bca1ffbfe4c0.png)\n\n**Step 2**: We need to find the values of $x$ and $y$ such as the area\n\n$$\nA=xy\n$$\n\nis the greatest possible value.\n\n**Step 3**: This is subject to the constraint that the perimeter is $15.$ This gives the equation\n\n$$\n2x+2y=15.\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: We make one of the variables the subject in the constraint equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+2y & =15 \\\\ y & =\\frac{15}{2}-x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $y=\\frac{15}{2}-x$ in the expression $A=xy$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =x(\\frac{15}{2}-x) \\\\ A & =\\frac{15}{2}x-{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 5**: We solve the equation ${A}^{′}(x)=0.$ Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n{A}^{′}(x)=\\frac{15}{2}-2x,\n$$\n\nand solving for the stationary points, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{′}(x) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{15}{2}-2x & =0 \\\\ 2x & =\\frac{15}{2} \\\\ x & =\\frac{15}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 6**: We confirm that $x=\\frac{15}{4}$ is a maximum using the second derivative test. The second derivative is\n\n$$\n{A}^{″}(x)=-2\\,⟹\\,{A}^{″}(\\frac{15}{4})=-2<0.\n$$\n\nSince ${A}^{″}(\\frac{15}{4})$ is negative, we conclude that $x=\\frac{15}{4}$ is indeed a maximum of $A(x).$\n\nFinally, when $x=\\frac{15}{4}$, we have \n\n$$\ny=\\frac{15}{2}-\\frac{15}{4}=\\frac{15}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the dimensions of the rectangle with the largest area are $x=\\frac{15}{4}$ and $y=\\frac{15}{4},$ and we conclude that\n\n$$\nA=xy=\\frac{15}{4}\\cdot \\frac{15}{4}≈14.06\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399426 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399427 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399426 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399428 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399426 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399429 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399426 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399430 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399426 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399431 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399426 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399426 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399426 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399430