s subinterval.\n\n- On the subinterval $[3,4],$ we have $g(3)=1$ and $g(4)=-3.$ Since $-1\\in [-3,1],$ the IVT *does* guarantee a solution to the equation $g(x)=-1$ on this subinterval.\n\n- On the subinterval $[4,5],$ we have $g(4)=-3$ and $g(5)=1.$ Since $-1\\in [-3,1],$ the IVT *does * guarantee a solution to the equation $g(x)=-1$ on this subinterval.\n\n- On the subinterval $[5,6],$ we have $g(5)=1$ and $g(6)=0.$ Since $-1\\notin [0,1],$ the IVT does *not* guarantee a solution to the equation $g(x)=-1$ on this subinterval.\n\n- On the subinterval $[6,7],$ we have $g(6)=0$ and $g(7)=2.$ Since $-1\\notin [0,2],$ the IVT does *not* guarantee a solution to the equation $g(x)=-1$ on this subinterval.\n\nThe IVT guarantees solutions to $g(x)=-1$ on the subintervals $[2,3],$ $[3,4]$  and $[4,5].$ Therefore, $g(x)=-1$ has at least three solutions on $[2,7].$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399496 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399497 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399496 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399498 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399496 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399496 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399496 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399501 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399496 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399496 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399496 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399497 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399496 1080 #uuid "5d82b2e4-6f95-5829-98a0-f3c805de2c17" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399497 1081 "3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399497 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399497 1084 #uuid "8858bd6f-a8b4-5fe8-a1a9-895135df061c" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399498 1081 "2" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399498 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 1319413